From 97d12a8cf294816194c0aacc141e5b8c61d3b926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:37:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [clangd] Module memos that did not change are not serialized
 again

The memo store (--module-memo-dir) wrote every 30 seconds by copying both
caches and building the JSON of every memo, and only then found that nothing
had changed since the last write. A process left idle did this all the time:
with a project's memos (30 MB of JSON), the allocator kept what each write
built and freed, and an idle clangd grew by hundreds of megabytes in ten
minutes.

A write now first compares the counts the caches' snapshots report with those
it last wrote, and copies and serializes nothing when they are the same. A
change made after the counts are read is written by the next write, as one
made after a snapshot was.
